      "title": "On-demand UI construction tools materialize working interfaces from natural-language task descriptions",
      "summary": "Large language models can now generate functional user interfaces on demand from natural-language task descriptions. A user explains what they are trying to accomplish, and the system materializes a working interface to support it.",
      "design_implication": "When a product designer types a task description to generate a working interface on demand, standard component libraries give way to fluid, real-time layout assembly. Designers shift from drawing static screens to orchestrating the underlying constraint rules that govern automated UI generation.",
